WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.520
A 48% higher dementia risk tracked frequent napping in 995 older adults. This is Longevity Weekly

00:00:06.520 --> 00:00:12.860
episode 4. The science of aging, read carefully, never medical advice. John Hopkins researchers,

00:00:13.200 --> 00:00:19.000
writing through Mirage News, followed Medicare beneficiaries who were at least 65 and free of dementia

00:00:19.000 --> 00:00:25.380
when the National Health and Aging Trends study clock started in 2013. The Journal of Gerontology,

00:00:25.380 --> 00:00:30.920
medical sciences posted the observational paper online on October 5th and follow up

00:00:30.920 --> 00:00:35.800
brand as long as ten years. Frequent meant most days or every day set against

00:00:35.800 --> 00:00:40.580
people who rarely or never napped. After demographics, health conditions, night

00:00:40.580 --> 00:00:45.720
sleep length, daytime sleepiness, and an apnea risk measure. Falling asleep

00:00:45.720 --> 00:00:50.740
without meaning to carried a 39% higher risk and naps of 30 minutes or less

00:00:50.740 --> 00:00:54.600
carried a 40% higher risk that survived those same adjustments.

00:00:55.280 --> 00:00:59.340
Naps longer than 30 minutes looked weaker once nighttime sleep was in the model.

00:00:59.940 --> 00:01:03.880
And Adam Spira said the pattern may mark brain change rather than cause it.

00:01:04.440 --> 00:01:09.820
Wakefulness circuits can fail early in dementia and push napping up, and dropping diagnoses

00:01:09.820 --> 00:01:13.960
from the first five years left the frequent and unintentional links looking similar.

00:01:14.660 --> 00:01:19.740
Sanford Burnham Prebus put a different assumption under a microscope in aging cell on September

00:01:19.740 --> 00:01:23.860
27th, 2026, and signs daily carried the report.

00:01:24.480 --> 00:01:29.680
Caroline Coomsta said people often claim autophagy fades with age, yet the human evidence

00:01:29.680 --> 00:01:31.340
for that fade is very thin.

00:01:32.000 --> 00:01:38.480
Volunteers from age 23-72, reporting no chronic disease, gave blood and skin, and some

00:01:38.480 --> 00:01:42.660
skin cells were turned into induced neurons so three cell types could be compared.

00:01:43.300 --> 00:01:48.560
Cleanup activity rose, fell, or held steady depending on the cell and on sex, and the

00:01:48.560 --> 00:01:53.440
The write-up says a small study suggests gentle exercise may nudge older adults back toward

00:01:53.440 --> 00:01:54.580
a more youthful pattern.

00:01:55.280 --> 00:02:00.140
Tatiana Moreno noted growing interest in targeting that recycling system, and nothing

00:02:00.140 --> 00:02:02.080
in the report is a regulator approval.

00:02:03.141 --> 00:02:08.021
Science Daily also carried a nail comparison from the European Academy of Dermatology and

00:02:08.021 --> 00:02:10.141
Vineriology Congress 2026.

00:02:10.841 --> 00:02:13.681
The first controlled look at GLP1 medicines and nails.

00:02:14.721 --> 00:02:22.101
575 users were set against 1,329 people with type 2 diabetes or obesity who had never taken

00:02:22.101 --> 00:02:26.301
the drugs, drawn from France, the United States, Brazil, and Mexico.

00:02:27.141 --> 00:02:33.741
Detachment showed up in 39% of users and 9% of never users, more than fourfold, and discoloration

00:02:33.741 --> 00:02:35.921
in 46% versus 17.

00:02:36.641 --> 00:02:42.581
Any nail disorder was 66% against 53, and the report says weight loss alone did not fully

00:02:42.581 --> 00:02:47.961
explain the gap. The summary also ties the same medicines to hair loss and scalp inflammation.

00:02:48.641 --> 00:02:55.301
Ozempic, Wigovie, Monjaro, Zepbound, Victosa, and Trulicity are described as weight loss and diabetes

00:02:55.301 --> 00:03:01.421
drugs, not as approved aging drugs. Last week's clock claims for this class did not include these

00:03:01.421 --> 00:03:09.006
nail numbers. Nature Aging on October 12, 2026 reported a large post-mortem association study,

00:03:09.006 --> 00:03:15.126
not a clinic test, 107 brain DNA methylation sites tracked Alzheimer's pathology,

00:03:15.546 --> 00:03:18.146
38 of them replicated in an independent set,

00:03:18.626 --> 00:03:23.046
and methylation partly mediated the link from APOE genotype to diagnosis.

00:03:24.269 --> 00:03:28.389
Fight aging summarized a preprint in which an anti-sense oligonucleotide

00:03:28.389 --> 00:03:33.809
against MIR-128-3P restored muscle mass and function in aged mice.

00:03:34.429 --> 00:03:38.129
The same inhibition improved heart function and limited bad remodeling

00:03:38.129 --> 00:03:42.889
after a heart attack in mice, and it eases skeletal and heart muscle disease in mouse

00:03:42.889 --> 00:03:45.329
and pig models of Duchenne muscular dystrophy.

00:03:46.049 --> 00:03:51.689
mitochondrial programs rose and inflammatory and fibiotic signals fell, a pattern the authors

00:03:51.689 --> 00:03:54.009
compare with known longevity interventions.

00:03:54.489 --> 00:04:02.469
The MIR1281 locus sits in a human stretch of chromosome 2Q21.3, tied in genetic association

00:04:02.469 --> 00:04:06.629
data, to grip strength, lung function, and cardiometabolic traits.

00:04:06.629 --> 00:04:12.089
L&amp;A therapeutics is aiming first at severe uses such as heart muscle after a heart attack,

00:04:12.449 --> 00:04:15.329
and this report has no human result and no approval.

00:04:15.909 --> 00:04:21.529
This week's mechanism is sleep, and the largest measurement set starts with 5,407 adults

00:04:21.529 --> 00:04:23.109
in the sleep heart health study.

00:04:23.629 --> 00:04:29.829
Mean age was 63, the range ran from 45 to 99, and 52% were women.

00:04:30.529 --> 00:04:35.349
Home polysomnography plus questionnaires, published in the Journal of the American Geriatric

00:04:37.649 --> 00:04:49.189
The night breaks into N1, light sleep, N2, where spindles fire, N3, slow wave sleep and rapid eye movement sleep when the cortex is busy and most dreaming happens.

00:04:49.489 --> 00:05:04.849
A 2015 review in current topics in behavioral neurosciences describes healthy aging as less slow wave sleep and less of its power, fewer and smaller spindles, lower rapid eye movement density, a smaller circadian swing and a clock that runs earlier.

00:05:04.849 --> 00:05:12.509
mild cognitive impairment, cut sleep quality, slow wave sleep, spindles, and the share of rapid eye movement sleep further.

00:05:12.969 --> 00:05:17.669
And the same review describes a profound circadian break as Alzheimer's disease develops.

00:05:18.309 --> 00:05:21.649
In younger adults, sleep consolidates both facts and skills.

00:05:22.129 --> 00:05:30.029
In healthy aging, that review says fact memory still consolidates and sleep, while some skill tasks, including motor sequences, do not.

00:05:30.629 --> 00:05:35.449
Fragmented sleep can blunt consolidation in the young, and more fragmentation with age

00:05:35.449 --> 00:05:37.129
may explain part of the change.

00:05:37.689 --> 00:05:42.629
Spindles in slow wave sleep are the features most tightly tied to consolidation, and both

00:05:42.629 --> 00:05:46.329
shrink again from mild cognitive impairment into Alzheimer's disease.

00:05:46.949 --> 00:05:51.529
Back in the sleep heart health study, older age meant shorter sleep, worse efficiency,

00:05:51.829 --> 00:05:53.489
and more arousals in men and women.

00:05:54.009 --> 00:05:59.049
Men specifically showed more stage 1 and stage 2 and less slow wave and rapid eye movement

00:05:59.049 --> 00:06:04.749
sleep. Women's stage pattern was a weaker straight line. Complaints ran the other way, older

00:06:04.749 --> 00:06:09.729
age did not track poor subjective sleep in men, while older women had more trouble falling

00:06:09.729 --> 00:06:15.149
asleep, with a trend toward waking at night and waking too early. Self-report and the machine

00:06:15.149 --> 00:06:20.129
agreed only modestly on sleep time and how long it took to fall asleep. Correlations

00:06:20.129 --> 00:06:27.349
from 0.06 to 0.32. Extra chronic disease, including sleep apnea, did not account for the

00:06:27.349 --> 00:06:29.389
age pattern or for those sex differences.

00:06:29.809 --> 00:06:34.949
A 2022 systematic review in the International Journal of Environmental Research and Public

00:06:34.949 --> 00:06:41.749
Health gathered 71 studies with sample mean ages from 58.3 to 93.7.

00:06:42.109 --> 00:06:46.269
33 were subjective, 31 objective, and 10 used both.

00:06:46.849 --> 00:06:51.089
Pathological aging looked worse than healthy older age on both kinds of measure.

00:06:51.589 --> 00:06:56.669
In Alzheimer's disease and mild cognitive impairment, rapid eye movement sleep, efficiency,

00:06:56.669 --> 00:07:00.249
latency, latency, and duration were the pieces most often off.

00:07:00.529 --> 00:07:05.649
The reviewers read severity as following the cognitive decline, and objective measures

00:07:05.649 --> 00:07:07.649
as more consistent than questionnaires.

00:07:08.329 --> 00:07:14.349
Men born in 1953 in the Danish Metropolitan cohort, written up in sleep medicine, had

00:07:14.349 --> 00:07:19.829
thinking tests about a decade apart, 206 at the first wave, and 106 at the second.

00:07:19.829 --> 00:07:26.529
baseline polysomnography covered 176 men and spindle slow wave and coherence

00:07:26.529 --> 00:07:31.949
analyses only 82 with enough non-rapid eye movement sleep. Trail making tests be

00:07:31.949 --> 00:07:37.629
slowed by 6.1 seconds and the symbol digit modalities test dropped 2.3 points.

00:07:38.149 --> 00:07:42.209
Better sleep efficiency went with better maintenance of cognition. More wake

00:07:42.209 --> 00:07:46.169
after sleep onset and a higher arousal index went with poorer memory and

00:07:46.169 --> 00:07:53.489
learning. More N1 went with poor executive function. N2 and N3 went the other way. Fast spindle

00:07:53.489 --> 00:07:58.549
size and frequency, slow wave features, and coherence in N2 and rapid eye movement sleep

00:07:58.549 --> 00:08:04.149
tracked processing speed, attention, and global scores. Those were spearmen correlations

00:08:04.149 --> 00:08:09.129
with a multiple testing correction, and the authors called them exploratory. They do not

00:08:09.129 --> 00:08:15.169
claim a forecast of neurodegenerative disease. Molecular psychiatry reported 24 older adults

00:08:15.169 --> 00:08:24.189
without dementia, mean age 71.29, 58.33% women, a quarter with amnestic mild cognitive impairment.

00:08:24.649 --> 00:08:31.549
They had lab polysomnography, cognitive testing, MRI, and a FOBV pet scan of colonergic nerve

00:08:31.549 --> 00:08:37.269
endings. Those endings keep the cortex active in rapid eye movement sleep when other transmitter

00:08:37.269 --> 00:08:43.349
systems are nearly quiet. More EEG slowing in that stage over frontal, central, parietal,

00:08:43.349 --> 00:08:49.229
occipital and temporal leads, tracked colonurgic loss, especially in frontal parietal cortex

00:08:49.229 --> 00:08:55.049
and the medial temporal lobe, after sex was controlled. Split by sex and adjusted for age,

00:08:55.449 --> 00:09:01.609
the link sat mainly in medial temporal regions in women and in neocortex and men. Women also took up

00:09:01.609 --> 00:09:07.509
more tracer than men. The authors float that slowing as a possible marker of colonurgic loss before

00:09:07.509 --> 00:09:14.409
dementia. 24 people, one night, no diagnostic standard. The 2015 review adds that insomnia,

00:09:14.769 --> 00:09:20.529
obstructive sleep apnea, and narcolepsy can hurt sleep-dependent memory even without neurodegeneration,

00:09:20.849 --> 00:09:25.769
and that sleep disorders get more common with age and more common again with neurodegenerative

00:09:25.769 --> 00:09:32.349
disease. Rapid eye movement behavior disorder can come before Parkinson's disease. A 2018 review

00:09:32.349 --> 00:09:35.069
in sleep medicine reviews only proposes a model.

00:09:35.709 --> 00:09:40.549
Low-grade inflammation might sit between bad sleep, dysfunctional body fat, and cognitive

00:09:40.549 --> 00:09:44.349
decline, tangled with the circadian system and hormone resistance.

00:09:44.989 --> 00:09:50.289
None of these papers show that a nap, a short night, or a missing stage causes dementia, and

00:09:50.289 --> 00:09:52.769
none test whether changing sleep changes the trajectory.

00:09:53.549 --> 00:09:59.349
The decade-long microstructure result is men-only, 82 of them for the fine EEG measures.

00:09:59.349 --> 00:09:59.529
factors.

00:10:00.089 --> 00:10:03.749
Questionnaires and machines disagree, and they disagree differently by sex.

00:10:04.369 --> 00:10:09.369
No drug, device, or regulator decision about sleep as an aging treatment is evaluated here.

00:10:09.969 --> 00:10:14.909
The large study can say age tracks worse measured sleep in thousands of adults after the illnesses

00:10:14.909 --> 00:10:18.909
they could count, and it still cannot say what would happen if sleep were changed.

00:10:19.799 --> 00:10:24.339
One thing worth knowing is that frequent and unplanned naps showed up before many dementia

00:10:24.339 --> 00:10:28.999
diagnoses, which fits a marker of failing wakefulness at least as well as a cause.

00:10:29.559 --> 00:10:34.959
Another is that recycling inside healthy volunteer cells had no single direction with age, so

00:10:34.959 --> 00:10:37.279
a simple fade story is ahead of that evidence.

00:10:37.899 --> 00:10:42.799
A third is that a Congress comparison, not a randomized trial, found more nail trouble

00:10:42.799 --> 00:10:46.479
in GLP1 users than weight loss alone explained in that report.

00:10:47.079 --> 00:10:52.899
And postmortem methylation tracked Alzheimer pathology and partly sat between APOE and diagnosis.

00:10:52.899 --> 00:10:57.259
a biological association, rather than a clock a clinic has validated.

00:10:57.699 --> 00:11:01.919
That's longevity weekly. This show is education, not medical advice.

00:11:02.499 --> 00:11:05.199
Talk to your own clinician before acting on anything you heard.

00:11:05.719 --> 00:11:07.939
I'm Patrick and Vancouver. See you next week.

